<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Piyamaradu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Piyamaradu was a western Anatolian warlord of the 13th century BCE, known from Hittite texts such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tawagalawa-letter">Tawagalawa letter</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manapa-tarhunta">Manapa-Tarhunta</a> letter. Of uncertain origin, possibly a member of the royal house of Arzawa, he raided Hittite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> lands from bases such as Millawanda (Miletus) with the support of the king of Ahhiyawa, usually identified with the Mycenaean <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>. Hittite kings repeatedly failed to bring him to justice.</p></div>
